Relevant columns and why they matter  
• midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.total_flag – filter “A” (individual 5‑yr age groups).  
• midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.age_group_indicator – keep “‑” (closed 5‑yr bands).  
• midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.starting_age – keep 0, 5, 10, 15 to cover ages 0‑19.  
• midyear_population_5yr_age_sex.midyear_population – population of each 5‑yr band (both sexes).  
• midyear_population.country_code / country_name / year – join key & year filter.  
• midyear_population.midyear_population – total mid‑year population (all ages).  
Condition we will use everywhere: year = 2020.  

Below are ten progressively richer inspection / analysis queries (each limited so they are fast to run).  

```sql
-- 1. Peek at the 5‑year age‑group table
SELECT *
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Look only at 2020 rows to be sure the year exists
SELECT DISTINCT country_code, country_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. What 5‑year starting ages are present for 2020?
SELECT DISTINCT starting_age
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2020
ORDER BY starting_age
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Age‑group populations for one sample country in 2020
SELECT starting_age, ending_age, midyear_population
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2020
  AND country_code = 'US'
  AND total_flag = 'A'
  AND age_group_indicator = '-'
ORDER BY starting_age
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Compute U.S. population under 20 in 2020
SELECT country_name,
       SUM(midyear_population) AS pop_under20
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2020
  AND country_code = 'US'
  AND total_flag = 'A'
  AND age_group_indicator = '-'
  AND starting_age < 20
GROUP BY country_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Total 2020 mid‑year population for the U.S.
SELECT country_name,
       midyear_population AS total_pop
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population`
WHERE year = 2020
  AND country_code = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Join the two figures for the U.S. to get the percentage <20
WITH under20 AS (
  SELECT SUM(midyear_population) AS pop_under20
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
  WHERE year = 2020
    AND country_code = 'US'
    AND total_flag = 'A'
    AND age_group_indicator = '-'
    AND starting_age < 20
)
SELECT t.country_name,
       u.pop_under20,
       t.midyear_population AS total_pop,
       ROUND(100 * u.pop_under20 / t.midyear_population, 2) AS pct_under20
FROM under20 u, `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` t
WHERE t.year = 2020 AND t.country_code = 'US'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Under‑20 population for every country in 2020
SELECT country_code, country_name,
       SUM(midyear_population) AS pop_under20
FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
WHERE year = 2020
  AND total_flag = 'A'
  AND age_group_indicator = '-'
  AND starting_age < 20
GROUP BY country_code, country_name
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Combine under‑20 and total population, rank by % under20, show top 10
WITH under20 AS (
  SELECT country_code, SUM(midyear_population) AS pop_under20
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
  WHERE year = 2020
    AND total_flag = 'A'
    AND age_group_indicator = '-'
    AND starting_age < 20
  GROUP BY country_code
)
SELECT t.country_name,
       u.pop_under20,
       t.midyear_population AS total_pop,
       ROUND(100 * u.pop_under20 / t.midyear_population, 2) AS pct_under20
FROM under20 u
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` t
  ON u.country_code = t.country_code
WHERE t.year = 2020
ORDER BY pct_under20 DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER QUERY – top 10 countries in 2020 with highest % of population <20
WITH under20 AS (
  SELECT country_code,
         country_name,
         SUM(midyear_population) AS population_under20
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population_5yr_age_sex`
  WHERE year = 2020
    AND total_flag = 'A'          -- individual 5‑yr bands
    AND age_group_indicator = '-' -- closed 5‑yr bands
    AND starting_age < 20         -- ages 0‑19
  GROUP BY country_code, country_name
)
SELECT u.country_name,
       u.population_under20,
       t.midyear_population AS total_population,
       ROUND(100 * u.population_under20 / t.midyear_population, 2) AS pct_population_under20
FROM under20 u
JOIN `bigquery-public-data.census_bureau_international.midyear_population` t
  ON u.country_code = t.country_code
WHERE t.year = 2020
ORDER BY pct_population_under20 DESC
LIMIT 10;
```
